  "segments": [
    {
      "start_us": 340000,
      "end_us": 11780000,
      "text": "But the spotlight effect shows us that it's pretty likely that the people who you think are judging you or that are perceiving you"
    },
    {
      "start_us": 12170000,
      "end_us": 17190000,
      "text": "are potentially not actually wondering why you are alone at all."
    },
    {
      "start_us": 17290000,
      "end_us": 20070000,
      "text": "They're not wondering if you are meeting someone."
    },
    {
      "start_us": 20170000,
      "end_us": 22870000,
      "text": "They're not wondering if you have no friends."
    },
    {
      "start_us": 22970000,
      "end_us": 29910000,
      "text": "And even on a positive note, they probably aren't even labeling you as confident or as empowered."
    },
    {
      "start_us": 30010000,
      "end_us": 34740000,
      "text": "Because in reality, because of the spotlight effect,"
    },
    {
      "start_us": 35440000,
      "end_us": 38730000,
      "text": "they probably aren't actually thinking about you at all."
    },
    {
      "start_us": 38880000,
      "end_us": 42170000,
      "text": "So the spotlight effect is this idea in psychology"
    },
    {
      "start_us": 42530000,
      "end_us": 43760000,
      "text": "that we walk"
    },
    {
      "start_us": 44200000,
      "end_us": 46670000,
      "text": "around feeling like there is a"
    },
    {
      "start_us": 46820000,
      "end_us": 50110000,
      "text": "spotlight above us, that everyone is paying attention"
    },
    {
      "start_us": 50470000,
      "end_us": 53290000,
      "text": "to us, when in reality, they are"
    },
    {
